    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain unobstructed at all times could significantly improve emergency responder access and reduce response delays. Keeping the driveway clear of parked vehicles, equipment, or other obstructions would support simultaneous ingress and egress for emergency apparatus. Clearly marking the access point from the street frontage may assist responders in locating the entry under low-visibility or nighttime conditions. Given the limited rear access to the structures, communicating alternate foot-access pathways through the open terrain to local responders in advance could support tactical planning and personnel movement around the property during an emergency operation."
