    "recommendations": "Reducing brush and dense ground vegetation in the immediate zone surrounding the structure could meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce fuel continuity near the building. Creating and maintaining separation between shrubs, tree clusters, and the structure may reduce the opportunity for fire to move directly toward improvements. Managing vegetation along the access route would support firefighter ingress and egress during a fire event, as well as resident evacuation. Where shrubs are located adjacent to the structure, increasing horizontal spacing between individual plants and between shrubs and combustible portions of the building could reduce fuel continuity. Thinning ground vegetation within the immediate structure perimeter and extending cleared or reduced-fuel zones outward where feasible would support suppression operations and improve overall wildfire resilience. Ongoing vegetation management across the mixed cover present on the property may help maintain these improvements over time."
